{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 48, :comments ["<b>On the seventh day, the prince of the children of Ephraim.</b> And it was the Sabbath, for the first day was the first of the act of creation. And because Joseph observed the Sabbath before the Torah was given, as it is said: ״וטבוח טבח והכן״ — and there is no preparation except for the Sabbath, as it is said: ״והיה ביום הששי והכינו את אשר יביאו״. The Holy One, blessed be He, said to him: by virtue of this, your son will prepare his offering on the day of the Sabbath, for an individual's offering does not override the Sabbath. And this is what is written: ״לי גלעד ולי מנשה ואפרים מעוז ראשי יהודה מחוקקי״. And Resh Lakish said: if a person says to you, why did Elijah build a bamah on Mount Carmel at a time when bamot were forbidden? — ״לי גלעד״, i.e., it was by divine speech. And if a person says to you, Gideon did seven things: the worshipped bull, the set-aside bull, built an altar, cut wood from the asherah, offered a sacrifice at night, through himself without a priest, and among the idolatrous priests — everything he did, he did by divine inspiration, as it is said: ״ויהי בלילה ההוא ויאמר לו קח את פר השור אשר לאביך ועלית עולה בעצי האשרה אשר תכרות ובנית מזבח לה' אלהיך על ראש המעון הזה״. And that is what is written: ״לי מנשה״ — for Gideon was from the tribe of Menasseh. ״ואפרים מעוז ראשי״ — if a person says to you, Joshua profaned the Sabbath at Jericho — he did so by divine inspiration, as it is written: ״וסבותם את העיר״ etc. ״כה תעשו ששת ימים״ etc., and it is written: ״וביום השביעי תסובו את העיר שבע פעמים״, and it is impossible for seven days to pass without a Sabbath. And because he conquered it on the day of the Sabbath, he sanctified it, saying: let it be a consecrated completion for HaShem. And likewise now, He permitted the tribe of Ephraim to profane the Sabbath on account of an individual's offering. ״יהודה מחוקקי״ — if a person says to you, David transgressed a negative commandment — the Holy One, blessed be He, said: David, who comes from the tribe of Judah, taught the penitents like a scribe who teaches children, as it is said: ״אלמדה פושעים דרכיך וחטאים אליך ישובו״. And so it is concluded at the beginning of עבודה זרה: David was not fit for that deed with Bathsheba, but only in order to provide an opening for penitents."], :book :numbers, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {0 "The verse לי גלעד ולי מנשה וגו' (Psalms 108:8–9) is read here as a mnemonic proof-text, with each phrase keyed to a different biblical figure who acted by divine sanction against ordinary halakhic rules: לי גלעד → Elijah (from Gilead); לי מנשה → Gideon; ואפרים מעוז ראשי → Ephraim's Sabbath offering; יהודה מחוקקי → David."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:09:09.664390333Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}